<title>COLOMBIA: BP confirms Cupiagua &quot;sub-thrust&quot; zone.</title>
<headline>BP confirms Cupiagua &quot;sub-thrust&quot; zone.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum Co Plc issued a statement confirming that hydrocarbons had been discovered in a so-called &quot;sub-thrust&quot; zone beneath the giant Cupiagua oil field in Colombia's eastern plains.</p>
<p>The terse statement by BP's local subsidiary, BP Exploration Company (Colombia) Ltd, said exploration and evaluation of the underlying zone would begin early next year.</p>
<p>For the time being, BP said it had no comment regarding the zone's  potential crude oil reserves.</p>
<p>-- Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
</text>
